From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Map connected controllers to players in connection
 order (USCL_AUTO_PADS)

With USCL_AUTO_PADS set, every connected SDL game controller (USB or
Bluetooth) becomes players 1-8 in the order it was connected, mapped with
the same defaults as Configure Input -> Input Device: per-controller button
layout, Joy-Con pairs as one dual controller, and motion where the pad has
sensors. Joysticks without a game controller mapping (wheels, flight sticks)
are skipped. With no controller connected the settings are left alone.
---
diff --git a/src/input_common/drivers/sdl_driver.h b/src/input_common/drivers/sdl_driver.h
--- a/src/input_common/drivers/sdl_driver.h
+++ b/src/input_common/drivers/sdl_driver.h
@@ -56,6 +56,9 @@
 
     std::vector<Common::ParamPackage> GetInputDevices() const override;
 
+    /// USCL: connected game controllers (Joy-Con pairs as one), oldest connection first
+    std::vector<Common::ParamPackage> GetPadsInConnectionOrder();
+
     ButtonMapping GetButtonMappingForDevice(const Common::ParamPackage& params) override;
     AnalogMapping GetAnalogMappingForDevice(const Common::ParamPackage& params) override;
     MotionMapping GetMotionMappingForDevice(const Common::ParamPackage& params) override;
